sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-23> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch03-23: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.61" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.608"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.68"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The fish half of the claim can be tested with open age-length surveys timed through the year, and damping is a sharp extra prediction beyond 'growth is seasonal'. Those surveys still do not follow individuals, and the human half still lacks a public longitudinal counterpart to Daffner's cadet table. The claim is therefore testable for North Sea plaice and haddock, and only weakly for humans." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Fit seasonal increments of length or stature to a sine term whose amplitude declines as mean growth rate declines. A winter deficit that shrinks smoothly toward zero with age would support the damped-sine description; irregular seasonality, or an amplitude that does not damp, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Survey lengths are cross-sectional, so size-selective mortality is mixed with growth.", "Open human series rarely repeat the same individuals at half-year intervals across adolescence.", "Temperature, feeding and day length move together, so a pure annual sine is not isolated." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch03-23 by Grok 4.7: 0.75" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-23> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-23--grok--operationalizability> .
